  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Maryland for FY2026 to date total $26.9B. Maryland has 74,509 awards so far, and the average award size is $361K. Obligations fell 32.3% year over year. Historical annual obligations show variation: FY21 was $39.2B, FY22 was $42.1B, FY23 was $41.7B, FY24 was $46.3B, and FY25 was $39.7B. The largest buying agency so far is the Department of Defense with $11B. Other major buying agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services with $5.3B and the Department of Energy with $1.9B. The top vendor is THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC with $1.5B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations with $3.1B, and Engineering Services and Computer Systems Design Services follow with $2.9B and $2.8B respectively.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting activity in Maryland changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 32.3% year over year. FY26 to date obligations total $26.9B, down from FY25 obligations of $39.7B. Annual obligations ranged from $39.2B in FY21 to $46.3B in FY24. The state has recorded 74,509 awards so far in FY26 to date, with an average award size of $361K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers, vendors, and industries in Maryland federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $11B, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $5.3B and the Department of Energy with $1.9B. THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC is the top vendor with $1.5B, and ORANO FEDERAL SERVICES LLC and AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC each have $900M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) leads industries with $3.1B, followed by Engineering Services at $2.9B and Computer Systems Design Services at $2.8B."
      }
    ]
  },
